[00:00.97] The scent grows richer
[00:03.33] He knows he must be near
[00:07.18] He finds a long passageway
[00:10.82] Lit by chandelier
[00:14.34] Each step he takes, the perfumes change
[00:18.72] From familiar fragrance to flavors strange
[00:22.91] A magnificent chamber
[00:26.47] Meets his eye
[00:29.94] 
[00:38.36] Inside, a long rose-water pool
[00:41.65] Is shrouded by fine mist
[00:45.71] Stepping in the moist silence
[00:48.88] With a warm breeze he's gently kissed
[00:53.23] Thinking he is quite alone
[00:57.20] He enters the room as if it were his own
[01:00.83] But ripples on the sweet pink water
[01:04.23] Reveal some company unthought of
[01:08.67] Rael stands astonished doubting his sight
[01:13.29] Struck by beauty, gripped in fright
[01:18.11] Three vermilion snakes of female face
[01:23.42] The smallest motion, filled with grace
[01:28.43] Muted melodies fill the echoing hall
[01:35.53] But there is no sign of warnin
[01:40.30] In the siren's call
[01:45.19] "Rael welcome, we are the Lamia of the pool"
[01:53.66] "We have been waiting for our waters to bring you cool"
[02:01.68] 
[02:41.96] Putting fear beside him
[02:45.75] He trusts in beauty blind
[02:49.01] He slips into the nectar
[02:52.37] Leaving his shredded clothes behind
[02:56.91] With their tongues, they test, taste and judge
[03:01.33] All that is mine
[03:04.44] They move in a series of caresses
[03:08.14] That glide up and down my spine
[03:11.51] 
[03:20.32] As they nibble the fruit of my flesh
[03:23.75] I feel no pain
[03:27.19] Only a magic
[03:30.64] That a name would stain
[03:34.96] With the first drop of my blood in their veins
[03:38.75] Their faces are convulsed in mortal pains
[03:42.09] The fairest cries "We all have loved you Rael"
[03:50.22] Each empty snakelike body floats
[03:54.97] Silent sorrow in empty boats
[04:00.57] A sickly sourness fills the room
[04:05.15] The bitter harvest of a dying bloom
[04:10.17] Looking for motion I know I will not find
[04:16.91] I stroke the curls now turning pale, in which I'd lain entwined
[04:27.07] "Oh Lamia, your flesh that remains I will take as my food"
[04:35.14] "It is the scent of garlic that lingers on my chocolate fingers"
[04:43.08] 
[05:25.70] Looking behind me
[05:28.97] The water turns icy blue
[05:32.16] The lights are dimmed
[05:34.33] And once again the stage is set for you
[05:40.20] 